                <note rend="inline" type="source">860P.512 Residence/30</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Latvia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1931-12-15"
                            >December 15, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received December 30.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8322</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the penultimate paragraph
                    of the Department’s Instruction No. 882, dated November 17, 1931, I have the
                    honor to report that the British consul in Riga informed the Legation verbally
                    today, that British subjects are now paying an annual sojourn tax in Latvia of
                    two Lats.</p>
                <p>American citizens, it will be recalled, are charged a registration fee of two
                    lats per annum.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Felix Cole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
